-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.

--
-- turtle-agent faf84c43 (fix/route-order-dire_maul_west): `plan-export --gm-cross-direct --floor-aware --approach-hops
-- --mmaps <the server's mmaps> --rev faf84c43 --stamp 20261115190000`. Dire Maul West route order fix (issue #1542): the
-- same six bosses in the same order, the same five crystal holds; 21 packs move to the leg whose boss-to-boss walk passes
-- them, five leg `to` rows and three approach lists move onto that walk, and 25 groups go (the west hall, the courtyard's
-- east side and the hall's north-west - 40 to 190 yd off every leg's walk - and four duplicate pulls of a pack another leg
-- already pulls). 208 steps (215 rows) instead of the deployed 467 (a fresh export of the old order: 521), 5,940 yd
-- instead of 15,685 (15,677 fresh); the straight route is 3,872 yd. The turtle-agent commit message names the row behind
-- each moved point. The key need row of door 300601 moves to leg 4 in 20261026130000: the corridor point 46.1333 500.5332
-- is 4.5 yd from the door, and that is the leg that walks it. plan-check: 228 points, 197 lint findings (71 fail) against
-- the old order's 339 points and 351 (92 fail); plan-probe: 5,940.4 yd, 8 backtracks (1,182 yd) against 15,677.3 / 31
-- (9,112); trash-check: no pack the walk wakes that the old rows did not pull.
-- dire_maul_west: map 429, 6 legs, 208 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_west';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_west';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_west';
